{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Candidate node.ad3ed6f7c586444ec7213491 adds NAV > 0 to legal scope without source support. This blocks even an established SFC designation when NAV is missing or nonpositive. Treat valuation validity separately from the circular's scope and the independent designation route.",
    "For positive NAV and exact common units, doubling combined exposure implements the inclusive 50% threshold. The source does not establish the supplied exposure methodology, valuation conventions, look-through rules or treatment of temporary crossings.",
    "Footnote 7 locates discretionary assessment below 50% of NAV. Using an actual applicable designation as an alternative classification basis preserves the outcome, but must not imply an unrestricted power newly inferred from this formula or permit risk factors alone to establish designation.",
    "Neither candidate implements exposure classification or measurement. Supplied Boolean or numerical facts require evidence; their declarations do not establish the underlying legal or valuation judgments.",
    "The three unbound dependency IDs have no identifiable authority mapping or non-null source hash. None can be treated as available or assigned to a named missing authority by guesswork.",
    "The supplied circular does not establish effective dates, persistence after exposure changes or designation withdrawal rules. Assessment-time inputs do not resolve those questions."
  ],
